From 0bfd43d7fcbc6526c4c748fe2d7e624809c0f637 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:53:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show every evolution route in the chart's detail view

The detail view drew only a species' path row: 6 "to" and 5 "from" slots.
A Baby II's Rookies past its 6 slots (Koromon's Candlemon, Solarmon, Kotemon,
Renamon and Guilmon), the Fresh and Ultimate pairs (Megadramon and Gigadramon
to Machinedramon, Meteormon to Boltmon...) and the parents of an original
without a path row (Gigadramon, Meteormon, ShogunGekomon...) had no box.

chartBuildLists gathers them in order without repeats; DIGI.DAT's chart block
lists the parents no row holds. The "to" side shows six boxes a page: the
cursor turns the page past the first or last box, a bar at the right shows
where it is. Each side is centred on the original layouts. The builder lives
in the menu overlay, loaded while the Player menu is open.
